1
00:00:08,620 --> 00:00:12,125
The train heading from Lonpur to
Dhanbad is ready to leave...

2
00:00:12,150 --> 00:00:14,230
MADHAVGARH

3
00:00:14,253 --> 00:00:15,953
Did you have to
visit Bihar for a trip?

4
00:00:16,313 --> 00:00:17,426
Why?

5
00:00:17,900 --> 00:00:19,460
What's wrong with Bihar?

6
00:00:21,700 --> 00:00:22,840
Wait...

7
00:00:23,073 --> 00:00:25,233
You should ask what
is right with Bihar?

8
00:00:25,640 --> 00:00:30,167
Gang wars, caste wars,
Maoists, Naxals

9
00:00:31,087 --> 00:00:32,480
and God knows what else.

10
00:00:34,640 --> 00:00:35,847
You didn't tell me,

11
00:00:36,473 --> 00:00:39,320
where did this sudden
love for Bihar come from?

12
00:00:41,847 --> 00:00:43,780
Hey, get in.

13
00:00:46,027 --> 00:00:48,033
Hey! Get in!

14
00:00:49,067 --> 00:00:50,107
Give me your bag!

15
00:00:50,980 --> 00:00:52,033
Let's go.

16
00:00:53,547 --> 00:00:54,553
Get in.

17
00:01:16,233 --> 00:01:18,906
Look brother, I don't want
to be anyone's son-in-law

18
00:01:19,030 --> 00:01:22,384
I am too old to get married.
I am the wrong choice for this.

19
00:01:22,993 --> 00:01:26,926
I have blood pressure and diabetes,
I am telling you I am useless.

20
00:01:27,187 --> 00:01:28,887
They know you are useless.

21
00:01:29,460 --> 00:01:31,353
This is not a gang that abducts
people and gets them married.

22
00:01:31,467 --> 00:01:33,320
Then who are they?
Why are they kidnapping us?

23
00:01:33,880 --> 00:01:35,526
Just wait and you will
have your answer.

24
00:01:38,780 --> 00:01:39,867
Come on. Get out.

25
00:01:44,920 --> 00:01:46,000
Okay, okay.

26
00:01:49,287 --> 00:01:50,580
Who is that?

27
00:01:59,940 --> 00:02:00,973
Baabi.

28
00:02:02,940 --> 00:02:06,073
You broke our pact Bhombol.
This is not done.

29
00:02:06,893 --> 00:02:08,473
What kind of a welcome is this?

30
00:02:09,200 --> 00:02:11,893
I sent a car and security.
You could thank me, you know?

31
00:02:12,733 --> 00:02:14,200
What about a garland? A band?

32
00:02:16,580 --> 00:02:18,160
Why do you look like a mess?

33
00:02:18,693 --> 00:02:20,740
How long has it been since
your last haircut?

34
00:02:21,587 --> 00:02:23,127
Excuse me. Wait a minute.

35
00:02:23,673 --> 00:02:25,168
Baabi? Bhombol?

36
00:02:25,193 --> 00:02:26,327
Why don't you call Mom?

37
00:02:26,400 --> 00:02:29,260
If I call her all the time then she
will leave everything in my name.

38
00:02:30,173 --> 00:02:33,580
Did you forget? I might be useless
but I am Mom's favourite.

39
00:02:34,680 --> 00:02:36,293
You are brothers!

40
00:02:37,060 --> 00:02:39,426
That is what Mom says but

41
00:02:39,550 --> 00:02:42,270
I think this is a case of a rainy night
and orphanage and the father of a church.

42
00:02:43,727 --> 00:02:45,553
Jayavrat this is my
brother - Mrinmoy.

43
00:02:45,793 --> 00:02:46,860
Same genes...

44
00:02:47,107 --> 00:02:48,587
but I think he got
all the coward genes.

45
00:02:49,253 --> 00:02:50,793
-Hi, I am Jay--
-New roommate.

46
00:02:51,107 --> 00:02:52,707
-Yes.
-Jayavrat.

47
00:02:53,367 --> 00:02:54,480
Jayavrat Saini.

48
00:02:57,040 --> 00:02:58,080
Bhombol?

49
00:02:58,687 --> 00:02:59,780
Are you getting married?

50
00:03:01,253 --> 00:03:03,273
An MLA's daughter
is getting married.

51
00:03:06,140 --> 00:03:07,153
What are they serving in
the buffet?

52
00:03:07,213 --> 00:03:09,413
Scandal. Sex scandal,

53
00:03:10,070 --> 00:03:14,170
extortion, bribery,
hidden cameras, blackmail,

54
00:03:14,580 --> 00:03:15,660
And dessert?

55
00:03:16,253 --> 00:03:17,453
Politicians.

56
00:03:20,327 --> 00:03:21,700
Now I am hungry.

57
00:03:24,193 --> 00:03:26,180
In these few districts of Bihar

58
00:03:26,587 --> 00:03:29,767
gang wars are a
frequent occurence.

59
00:03:30,660 --> 00:03:33,253
That's not even mentioning the
caste issues and Maoist troubles.

60
00:03:34,627 --> 00:03:37,940
In fact, 6 months ago there
was a huge massacre.

61
00:03:39,160 --> 00:03:42,167
And now all of a sudden...
In the middle of all this...

62
00:03:42,973 --> 00:03:47,587
We have an extortion
and blackmailing case...

63
00:03:48,393 --> 00:03:50,027
Now my plate is full.

64
00:03:51,787 --> 00:03:53,000
That is why I called you.

65
00:03:53,987 --> 00:03:54,987
Get to work.

66
00:03:56,173 --> 00:03:57,260
Enjoy.

67
00:03:58,047 --> 00:03:59,120
See you.

68
00:04:09,127 --> 00:04:10,327
Hey Shekhar...

69
00:04:11,367 --> 00:04:13,647
Don't you think your brother...

70
00:04:13,927 --> 00:04:17,327
Bhombol looks a bit like me?

71
00:04:34,260 --> 00:04:36,367
By the way, what
does your brother do?

72
00:04:37,747 --> 00:04:38,827
I can tell you

73
00:04:39,367 --> 00:04:40,747
but then I will have to kill you.

74
00:04:41,380 --> 00:04:42,533
Oh my.

75
00:04:44,753 --> 00:04:46,860
Well, I need a drink.

76
00:04:54,800 --> 00:04:57,493
The bar is very crowded I literally
had to fight for this scotch.

77
00:04:57,527 --> 00:04:58,713
It's fake.

78
00:05:02,753 --> 00:05:04,133
It was smuggled in from Nepal.

79
00:05:08,873 --> 00:05:11,953
If you want the real thing then the
drivers are drinking Mahua outside.

80
00:05:12,280 --> 00:05:13,487
Go there.

81
00:05:14,647 --> 00:05:16,433
I can't believe they
gave me fake alcohol.

82
00:05:18,320 --> 00:05:19,760
Impressive.

83
00:05:25,280 --> 00:05:26,953
Did you know already...

84
00:05:27,747 --> 00:05:28,900
or was it just guesswork?

85
00:05:32,533 --> 00:05:33,900
Guessing is hardly any work.

86
00:05:36,867 --> 00:05:37,867
I see.

87
00:05:39,227 --> 00:05:40,453
This will be fun.

88
00:05:45,773 --> 00:05:49,513
Were you invited to the wedding
or did you come for the free food?

89
00:05:56,873 --> 00:05:58,500
No, I came to enjoy the clarinet.

90
00:06:00,880 --> 00:06:04,213
You play a string instrument but
you came to enjoy the clarinet?

91
00:06:10,827 --> 00:06:12,253
Rough fingernails...

92
00:06:13,480 --> 00:06:16,167
and the corn on the right
hand because of the bow.

93
00:06:16,793 --> 00:06:17,993
Good observation.

94
00:06:18,740 --> 00:06:21,207
-Your good name?
-It is a very good name.

95
00:06:23,880 --> 00:06:25,760
My name,by the way,
is Shekhar Home.

96
00:06:26,953 --> 00:06:28,007
Shekhar Home.

97
00:06:28,367 --> 00:06:29,553
Nice to meet you.

98
00:06:33,073 --> 00:06:34,607
Yeah... Nice... nice...

99
00:06:40,607 --> 00:06:43,680
And... what... is your name?

100
00:06:44,513 --> 00:06:45,740
Iraboty!

101
00:06:54,367 --> 00:06:55,553
See you later?

102
00:06:58,673 --> 00:07:00,793
No... I doubt it.

103
00:07:10,580 --> 00:07:11,847
I dug this out myself.

104
00:07:14,073 --> 00:07:15,187
I see you're socialising.

105
00:07:15,390 --> 00:07:16,830
No... just...

106
00:07:20,720 --> 00:07:22,060
Are you sure you
don't want to drink?

107
00:07:22,113 --> 00:07:24,660
I don't... I...
No... I don't.

108
00:07:25,073 --> 00:07:26,367
You should you know.

109
00:07:27,047 --> 00:07:28,860
They say alcohol
is a social lubricant.

110
00:07:29,840 --> 00:07:31,040
Yes. John Kouriskey.

111
00:07:32,853 --> 00:07:34,153
Not bad.

112
00:07:41,373 --> 00:07:43,080
Hey, isn't that...

113
00:07:43,140 --> 00:07:45,273
Iraboty. I mean, I don't know
who she is...

114
00:08:26,113 --> 00:08:28,493
She is the one singing but you're the
one standing with your mouth open.

115
00:09:18,040 --> 00:09:19,140
Come in.

116
00:09:24,527 --> 00:09:26,313
You already know Mr. Yadav.

117
00:09:26,900 --> 00:09:28,400
This is Mr. Jitendra Jha.

118
00:09:28,747 --> 00:09:30,227
That is Mr. Sushil Pandey.

119
00:09:31,053 --> 00:09:32,913
Honourable members of
the Bihar State Assembly.

120
00:09:33,520 --> 00:09:36,420
Congratulations on your
daughter's wedding Mr. Yadav.

121
00:09:36,953 --> 00:09:38,293
This is a great function.

122
00:09:38,367 --> 00:09:39,367
Can we start?

123
00:09:41,080 --> 00:09:42,247
Go fetch it.

124
00:10:10,527 --> 00:10:13,587
Post two men outside his home
on Bailey Road, in Bidya Colony.

125
00:10:14,373 --> 00:10:17,860
-Yes.
-Make them sit outside with a gun.

126
00:10:18,207 --> 00:10:22,533
And if anyone causes any
trouble you shoot them dead.

127
00:10:22,893 --> 00:10:24,133
-Understand?
-Yes sir.

128
00:10:26,680 --> 00:10:29,127
If anyone tries to file
a complaint against me

129
00:10:29,887 --> 00:10:31,160
then you should inform me.

130
00:10:31,527 --> 00:10:35,133
Then I will handle where to
dispose of their bodies.

131
00:10:35,953 --> 00:10:37,573
-Understand?
-Yes sir.

132
00:10:39,300 --> 00:10:40,480
Where is the love letter?

133
00:10:42,033 --> 00:10:43,073
Love letter...

134
00:10:43,467 --> 00:10:44,493
Ransom note.

135
00:10:49,873 --> 00:10:51,433
YOU MUST PAY THE PRICE

136
00:10:55,647 --> 00:10:57,213
You must pay the price?

137
00:10:58,367 --> 00:11:01,267
This sounds like a dialogue
from a Dharmendra movie.

138
00:11:01,513 --> 00:11:02,933
'Pratigya'.

139
00:11:04,540 --> 00:11:06,087
This is not a dialogue
from 'Pratigya'.

140
00:11:09,333 --> 00:11:11,773
But the question still remains

141
00:11:12,180 --> 00:11:13,520
the price for what?

142
00:11:17,733 --> 00:11:20,320
Who was the Heroine in 'Pratigya'?

143
00:11:20,767 --> 00:11:21,913
-Hema Malini.
-Hema Malini.

144
00:11:22,873 --> 00:11:24,000
She...

145
00:11:26,027 --> 00:11:27,267
Hey! Shekhar!

146
00:11:29,187 --> 00:11:30,207
Shekhar!

147
00:11:32,550 --> 00:11:33,910
What happened?

148
00:11:46,100 --> 00:11:49,867
Are you crazy? There are MLA's waiting
for us inside and you're chasing a girl?

149
00:11:50,653 --> 00:11:53,807
Hema Malini is not
the Heroine in our film,

150
00:11:55,127 --> 00:11:56,180
she is the villain.

151
00:12:09,300 --> 00:12:11,206
Where have you brought
me so early in the morning?

152
00:12:11,240 --> 00:12:12,887
You didn't even let me drink tea.

153
00:12:17,393 --> 00:12:18,520
Hey!

154
00:12:19,407 --> 00:12:21,013
Shekhar this is illegal.

155
00:12:32,100 --> 00:12:33,880
It's locked. There is no one here.
Let's go.

156
00:12:46,793 --> 00:12:49,193
What? Are you conducting a
structural analysis?

157
00:12:49,513 --> 00:12:51,167
-What is going on here?
-Let's go soldier.

158
00:12:51,687 --> 00:12:53,447
-Let's go.
-Let's go.

159
00:12:54,413 --> 00:12:55,973
-Let's go!
-Hey.

160
00:12:57,140 --> 00:12:58,193
Hey Shekhar?

161
00:12:58,660 --> 00:12:59,833
Let's go.

162
00:13:02,830 --> 00:13:04,274
What were you even
doing in the army?

163
00:13:04,299 --> 00:13:06,546
Even in the army
I was just a doctor.

164
00:13:14,147 --> 00:13:15,273
Come.

165
00:13:22,840 --> 00:13:24,847
Whose house are
we breaking into?

166
00:13:30,840 --> 00:13:33,306
What are we doing here Shekhar?
Will you tell me something?

167
00:13:45,940 --> 00:13:47,373
Oh my God!

168
00:13:48,293 --> 00:13:49,680
Now I understand.

169
00:13:51,827 --> 00:13:53,227
Now go look for the tapes.

170
00:13:53,473 --> 00:13:54,673
There are a lot of cupboards.

171
00:13:55,433 --> 00:13:57,740
But why would she hide
the proof in her own house?

172
00:13:57,893 --> 00:13:59,713
It's safe, secure and accessible.

173
00:14:00,220 --> 00:14:02,072
But don't ask questions.
Get on the job.

174
00:14:07,093 --> 00:14:08,213
Room.

175
00:14:13,367 --> 00:14:15,493
-There is nothing in that room.
-Check that one.

176
00:14:16,707 --> 00:14:18,727
-That room.
-Will you stay in this room?

177
00:14:19,200 --> 00:14:20,633
Shhh.

178
00:14:24,460 --> 00:14:25,720
That room.

179
00:14:34,540 --> 00:14:35,600
Shekhar!

180
00:14:39,567 --> 00:14:41,100
Should we start the matinee show?

181
00:15:01,093 --> 00:15:03,886
It looks like she is her own
biggest fan just like you,

182
00:15:03,911 --> 00:15:05,353
don't you think so?

183
00:15:06,560 --> 00:15:07,813
Ask her yourself.

184
00:15:09,953 --> 00:15:10,953
What do you mean?

185
00:15:24,027 --> 00:15:25,027
Want some tea?

186
00:15:25,173 --> 00:15:26,380
I don't mind.

187
00:15:28,993 --> 00:15:30,013
Don't be scared.

188
00:15:31,400 --> 00:15:32,480
It's not poisoned.

189
00:15:33,567 --> 00:15:36,053
Drink it before it gets cold or
it will taste like sherbet.

190
00:15:42,360 --> 00:15:43,833
Did you find anything in the tapes?

191
00:15:44,887 --> 00:15:46,300
Simmondsia Chinensis.

192
00:15:47,593 --> 00:15:49,640
Scientific name for Jojoba.

193
00:15:50,267 --> 00:15:51,933
It is a plant that
grows in deserts.

194
00:15:52,493 --> 00:15:54,127
It is the fragrance you give off.

195
00:15:54,733 --> 00:15:55,840
Nice to meet you.

196
00:16:03,187 --> 00:16:04,247
Wow.

197
00:16:05,510 --> 00:16:08,323
You didn't even give me a proper
handshake but you still know so much.

198
00:16:10,473 --> 00:16:13,193
Your hands held some
secret fragrances.

199
00:16:16,653 --> 00:16:18,240
Your homemade Jojoba oil.

200
00:16:24,980 --> 00:16:25,980
By the way,

201
00:16:27,367 --> 00:16:29,620
it's difficult to find this
oil in Bihar & Bengal

202
00:16:31,540 --> 00:16:33,360
You studied in
Rajasthan, didn't you?

203
00:16:34,920 --> 00:16:37,606
Your Gurukool (Music school)
was there.

204
00:16:39,453 --> 00:16:42,067
What else do they teach
other than music?

205
00:16:42,840 --> 00:16:46,067
Learning the ragas also
teaches you about pain.

206
00:16:50,753 --> 00:16:52,300
But you have everything.

207
00:16:53,160 --> 00:16:57,767
Beauty, money and fame then why
are you blackmailing the MLA's?

208
00:17:00,127 --> 00:17:01,293
For power?

209
00:17:02,680 --> 00:17:04,740
Even a light bulb holds power.

210
00:17:05,740 --> 00:17:09,440
The problem with power is that
it can be turned off with a switch.

211
00:17:10,240 --> 00:17:11,946
You don't want power...

212
00:17:12,107 --> 00:17:13,187
You already have money...

213
00:17:16,920 --> 00:17:18,233
So why do it?

214
00:17:22,487 --> 00:17:23,547
Interesting.

215
00:17:25,813 --> 00:17:28,047
Interesting! We should leave.

216
00:17:28,660 --> 00:17:31,787
I am sure Iraboty has a lot
more to do than just talk to us.

217
00:17:33,447 --> 00:17:34,447
Okay.

218
00:17:41,487 --> 00:17:42,633
Thank you.

219
00:17:43,000 --> 00:17:44,006
Sorry...

220
00:17:46,900 --> 00:17:47,986
See you later.

221
00:17:48,067 --> 00:17:49,160
I doubt it.

222
00:18:03,893 --> 00:18:05,033
Did you notice?

223
00:18:05,453 --> 00:18:08,767
As soon as I confronted her on
blackmailing the MLA's

224
00:18:09,080 --> 00:18:10,293
her face went pale.

225
00:18:10,520 --> 00:18:12,207
Whose phone call
was she waiting on?

226
00:18:13,080 --> 00:18:14,487
Phone? What phone?

227
00:18:14,747 --> 00:18:16,573
You just said you
noticed something.

228
00:18:19,260 --> 00:18:21,660
Didn't you notice that she was
waiting for someone to call?

229
00:18:22,047 --> 00:18:24,142
-Really?
-Really.

230
00:18:24,167 --> 00:18:27,248
Then at least we can get a list of
all the people who called her today.

231
00:18:27,310 --> 00:18:28,744
It has to be an opposition leader!

232
00:18:29,313 --> 00:18:31,667
She likes playing the game alone.

233
00:18:32,720 --> 00:18:34,047
Typical egoist.

234
00:18:34,847 --> 00:18:36,180
Brash, rude...

235
00:18:36,893 --> 00:18:38,047
narcissistic.

236
00:18:39,153 --> 00:18:40,587
Sounds like somebody else I know.

237
00:18:44,000 --> 00:18:46,607
Hey, isn't that your brother's car?

238
00:18:47,827 --> 00:18:49,887
Does he bring everyone
he kidnaps to this hotel?

239
00:18:51,533 --> 00:18:53,620
What do they say in English?

240
00:18:53,800 --> 00:18:55,093
Cat on a...

241
00:18:55,310 --> 00:18:56,497
Hot tin roof?

242
00:18:57,600 --> 00:18:59,693
Baabi, we got the ransom call.

243
00:18:59,767 --> 00:19:02,607
Three MLA's need to bring 20 kilos of
gold to the same place at the same time.

244
00:19:02,673 --> 00:19:03,680
We should leave immediately.

245
00:19:03,754 --> 00:19:04,845
20 kilos of gold?

246
00:19:04,870 --> 00:19:07,820
Yes and be careful they are
carrying more guns than gold.

247
00:19:08,007 --> 00:19:09,113
Let's go Shekhar.

248
00:19:10,853 --> 00:19:12,046
Baabi?

249
00:19:12,267 --> 00:19:13,973
What time did you
get the ransom call?

250
00:19:14,700 --> 00:19:15,853
At around 9:30.

251
00:19:17,927 --> 00:19:19,695
And at what time do you
need to be at the location?

252
00:19:19,720 --> 00:19:21,127
10:30. Which means right now.

253
00:19:22,840 --> 00:19:24,793
Which means the phone call
she was waiting for

254
00:19:25,627 --> 00:19:27,720
was not for the confirmation
of the ransom call.

255
00:19:27,853 --> 00:19:28,980
She?

256
00:19:29,920 --> 00:19:33,840
That's right, this means she already
knew the ransom calls have been made.

257
00:19:34,286 --> 00:19:35,927
She was waiting
for a different call?

258
00:19:36,140 --> 00:19:39,080
I don't understand what you're
trying to say... Who is she?

259
00:19:39,727 --> 00:19:41,127
And whose call?

260
00:19:44,433 --> 00:19:45,793
Where is the pick-up point?

261
00:19:53,000 --> 00:19:54,107
No one is coming here.

262
00:19:54,487 --> 00:19:55,913
What? Why?

263
00:19:56,400 --> 00:19:57,540
What is wrong?

264
00:19:58,653 --> 00:20:00,533
They don't want your gold.

265
00:20:02,007 --> 00:20:04,247
They just wanted to know
where you kept it.

266
00:20:08,787 --> 00:20:10,327
Where did you get this gold from?

267
00:20:11,507 --> 00:20:12,820
From a brick factory.

268
00:20:14,013 --> 00:20:15,307
From a gas godown.

269
00:20:15,987 --> 00:20:17,527
From my in-law's home.

270
00:20:18,560 --> 00:20:20,593
All three of these
places were the targets.

271
00:20:21,200 --> 00:20:23,160
Black money, gold,

272
00:20:23,206 --> 00:20:27,140
paperwork for properties which these
politicians can't store in banks

273
00:20:27,720 --> 00:20:29,420
are held in these safe-houses.

274
00:20:34,587 --> 00:20:36,100
Which got vandalised.

275
00:20:36,800 --> 00:20:39,380
But the MLA's still insist
that nothing is missing?

276
00:20:41,007 --> 00:20:42,351
Iraboty was waiting
for the phone call

277
00:20:42,375 --> 00:20:44,673
to inform her of when the MLA's
would leave their safe-houses.

278
00:20:45,693 --> 00:20:49,173
But she still hasn't found
what she is looking for.

279
00:20:50,087 --> 00:20:52,253
Okay, I will get Iraboty
picked up for questioning.

280
00:20:52,387 --> 00:20:53,687
You won't find anything.

281
00:20:54,200 --> 00:20:55,313
Why?

282
00:20:55,767 --> 00:20:57,787
Even though we know
that she is the blackmailer.

283
00:20:58,113 --> 00:20:59,713
On what basis will
you interrogate her?

284
00:21:00,300 --> 00:21:03,560
"The fact that you own Jojoba oil is
proof that you are the blackmailer,"

285
00:21:03,588 --> 00:21:05,261
will you say that to her?

286
00:21:06,380 --> 00:21:08,473
-Come on Baabi.
-Come on Bhombol.

287
00:21:11,767 --> 00:21:13,000
Take this.

288
00:21:15,793 --> 00:21:17,367
So what exactly does she want?

289
00:21:18,463 --> 00:21:20,583
There is a common connection
between all of those videos,

290
00:21:20,789 --> 00:21:23,380
find it and you will
know what she wants.

291
00:21:24,727 --> 00:21:25,973
Do you want to find out?

292
00:21:28,280 --> 00:21:29,820
Yes, of course.

293
00:21:30,920 --> 00:21:32,653
Okay then I will
head to Bailey Road

294
00:21:33,253 --> 00:21:34,647
and you head to Yadav's brothel.

295
00:21:35,527 --> 00:21:37,026
Why should I go to the brothel?

296
00:21:37,833 --> 00:21:38,987
I am an honest man.

297
00:21:39,413 --> 00:21:41,533
You go to the brothel and I
will head to Bailey Road.

298
00:21:42,060 --> 00:21:45,440
Oh my, my. "Honest man?"

299
00:21:59,920 --> 00:22:01,833
Oh sir! Please come in.

300
00:22:02,433 --> 00:22:06,240
Tell me, Bengali, Bihari,
Punjabi, Nepali, Gujarati...

301
00:22:06,573 --> 00:22:09,233
All available! There are
no charges just for looking.

302
00:22:09,473 --> 00:22:11,773
No... A Bihari-Bengali will do.

303
00:22:11,980 --> 00:22:14,460
-Malti...
-No, that's... one more thing...

304
00:22:14,580 --> 00:22:16,893
-If she wears a gajra in her hair...
-You want a Gajra?

305
00:22:17,060 --> 00:22:19,133
-Rinku!
-No, I already saw her...

306
00:22:19,633 --> 00:22:21,308
I also want a bindi on
her forehead. A big one.

307
00:22:21,430 --> 00:22:23,105
You want a gajra and a bindi?

308
00:22:23,167 --> 00:22:25,367
And if there was a
mole on her skin...

309
00:22:25,627 --> 00:22:28,866
Oh my! It looks like sir
is a connoisseur.

310
00:22:29,430 --> 00:22:31,853
Gajra, bindi and a mole!

311
00:22:32,573 --> 00:22:36,173
-Th... There is one more thing.
-Another? Go ahead.

312
00:22:37,670 --> 00:22:38,930
I want a leather belt.

313
00:22:40,040 --> 00:22:41,107
You won't get that.

314
00:22:41,293 --> 00:22:42,347
Really?

315
00:22:43,080 --> 00:22:44,453
So why don't you just send her?

316
00:22:59,640 --> 00:23:02,660
How many times have I told
you not to step outside? Come in.

317
00:23:06,540 --> 00:23:09,413
Hey! Hey! There is no need for that.
Put your clothes back on.

318
00:23:12,313 --> 00:23:14,620
Yes, yes, that's fine. Sit down.

319
00:23:22,633 --> 00:23:23,847
What is your name?

320
00:23:24,993 --> 00:23:26,913
-Sujata.
-And what is the mole girl's name?

321
00:23:27,707 --> 00:23:29,880
-You came from the MLA's office right?
-No I didn't.

322
00:23:29,940 --> 00:23:31,606
What is the name of
the girl with the mole?

323
00:23:32,520 --> 00:23:33,833
-Bimla.
-Where is Bimla?

324
00:23:34,920 --> 00:23:37,487
I am being honest,
I don't know where he is.

325
00:23:37,853 --> 00:23:40,620
Sir it's not about the money.
I really don't know.

326
00:23:41,070 --> 00:23:42,488
Did she say anything
before she left?

327
00:23:42,513 --> 00:23:45,260
No... she just suddenly
disappeared.

328
00:23:45,680 --> 00:23:47,453
I don't know where she went.

329
00:23:47,567 --> 00:23:49,693
You don't know where she went...
Do you know where she came from?

330
00:23:50,247 --> 00:23:51,500
She is from Begusarai.

331
00:23:54,833 --> 00:23:56,093
I have a problem Sujata.

332
00:23:57,440 --> 00:23:59,120
You know how some
people have pacemakers?

333
00:23:59,467 --> 00:24:00,913
I have a lie-detector in me.

334
00:24:02,520 --> 00:24:04,007
You see, lying is an art.

335
00:24:04,260 --> 00:24:06,080
There is sweat on your forehead,
your pupils are dilated

336
00:24:06,127 --> 00:24:08,240
your fingers are trembling,

337
00:24:09,380 --> 00:24:11,660
you need to control these things
before you start lying.

338
00:24:12,300 --> 00:24:13,580
Tell me, where is she from?

339
00:24:33,830 --> 00:24:36,350
KHORIDAI - 0 KM

340
00:24:37,107 --> 00:24:39,940
The Bat said to the Porcupine

341
00:24:39,965 --> 00:24:43,073
"We will see something fun tonight.

342
00:24:43,160 --> 00:24:46,993
The owl will come out to hunt,

343
00:24:48,347 --> 00:24:52,867
and the rat will face it's death..."

344
00:25:03,693 --> 00:25:04,880
Hello Bimla.

345
00:25:06,140 --> 00:25:07,380
What do you want?

346
00:25:08,180 --> 00:25:09,627
I want to meet someone.

347
00:25:09,680 --> 00:25:10,680
Who?

348
00:25:10,900 --> 00:25:12,960
The one who is standing
outside the door.

349
00:25:13,547 --> 00:25:14,767
Iraboty.

350
00:25:15,587 --> 00:25:18,047
Tell her I am here to help her.

351
00:25:20,400 --> 00:25:21,627
Help?

352
00:25:22,707 --> 00:25:24,360
You work for the MLA's.

353
00:25:27,320 --> 00:25:28,880
Your job was to capture me.

354
00:25:29,400 --> 00:25:30,725
If I wanted to do that

355
00:25:30,750 --> 00:25:33,310
then I would have brought
the police with me the other day.

356
00:25:38,740 --> 00:25:42,273
You did not find what
you were looking for.

357
00:25:42,940 --> 00:25:44,227
I know that.

358
00:25:45,600 --> 00:25:46,853
I want to help you.

359
00:25:48,267 --> 00:25:49,707
Go ahead, I am listening.

360
00:25:50,533 --> 00:25:51,860
Khoridai...

361
00:25:57,167 --> 00:25:59,280
It looks like a ghost village.

362
00:26:00,407 --> 00:26:01,793
There are widows everywhere

363
00:26:02,453 --> 00:26:05,380
and there are bullet
holes in the wall.

364
00:26:07,533 --> 00:26:12,267
So many people died and yet the
media doesn't even know about it.

365
00:26:13,253 --> 00:26:14,413
Why is that?

366
00:26:15,107 --> 00:26:16,500
Iraboty,

367
00:26:16,910 --> 00:26:19,969
a few months ago the people of
Khoridai protested against the MLA's

368
00:26:20,609 --> 00:26:22,523
those protests turned violent.

369
00:26:24,687 --> 00:26:26,093
Buses were burnt.

370
00:26:26,670 --> 00:26:28,393
Gandhi bhavan was ransacked.

371
00:26:28,418 --> 00:26:30,833
Highways were closed off for
two to three days.

372
00:26:31,000 --> 00:26:34,260
And so, to put an
end to the protests

373
00:26:34,310 --> 00:26:37,990
the MLA's brought
their thugs to Khoridai.

374
00:26:47,180 --> 00:26:50,793
Bimla's husband was
killed in this massacre.

375
00:26:56,433 --> 00:26:57,733
Bimla wanted revenge.

376
00:26:59,947 --> 00:27:01,013
You made a plan.

377
00:27:01,933 --> 00:27:06,213
Bimla went to the brothel
that Yadav visits frequently,

378
00:27:06,627 --> 00:27:09,120
she became Yadav's
favourite and then...

379
00:27:09,453 --> 00:27:10,553
the video.

380
00:27:11,320 --> 00:27:12,320
Right?

381
00:27:13,280 --> 00:27:16,280
You ran a sting operation on
the other two MLA's.

382
00:27:17,627 --> 00:27:18,808
And then?

383
00:27:18,833 --> 00:27:21,627
My assistant... my
partner will tell you the rest.

384
00:27:24,847 --> 00:27:26,147
No, no, no...

385
00:27:35,120 --> 00:27:36,120
Hello.

386
00:27:38,027 --> 00:27:39,053
Hello partner.

387
00:27:40,413 --> 00:27:41,713
So you got caught too?

388
00:27:42,453 --> 00:27:44,213
More like got myself caught.

389
00:27:44,487 --> 00:27:47,520
Anyway... what did you find out?

390
00:27:47,940 --> 00:27:49,733
Once I reached
Bailey Road, Vidya Colony

391
00:27:50,013 --> 00:27:52,207
I asked around
about those two thugs.

392
00:27:52,747 --> 00:27:53,860
Here you go.

393
00:27:55,733 --> 00:27:57,140
-Tell me something.
-Yes?

394
00:27:57,513 --> 00:28:00,180
Do these two spend all day here?

395
00:28:00,273 --> 00:28:01,647
Don't ask me sir.

396
00:28:02,627 --> 00:28:04,620
I will get killed for no
reason just like Pankaj.

397
00:28:07,033 --> 00:28:09,113
Pankaj who?
Tell me more.

398
00:28:10,640 --> 00:28:11,900
He was a great man.

399
00:28:12,593 --> 00:28:14,013
That is his house there.

400
00:28:15,553 --> 00:28:17,640
He was a journalist for
Swatantra Dainik newspaper.

401
00:28:17,840 --> 00:28:19,960
I went to the Swatantra
Dainik headquarters

402
00:28:20,033 --> 00:28:23,373
and found out that he was
working on a big story.

403
00:28:24,607 --> 00:28:28,587
That reporter Pankaj was here
on the day of the massacre.

404
00:28:29,607 --> 00:28:31,300
He took a lot of pictures.

405
00:28:33,193 --> 00:28:34,853
As soon as the MLA's found out

406
00:28:36,180 --> 00:28:38,807
they started pressuring him
not to release the story...

407
00:28:39,080 --> 00:28:40,353
but he didn't listen.

408
00:28:41,720 --> 00:28:45,300
The MLA's did what they
always do to shut someone up.

409
00:28:57,733 --> 00:29:02,413
But they still haven't found the
photos he took or their negatives.

410
00:29:02,600 --> 00:29:04,213
Hey, shut up!

411
00:29:04,473 --> 00:29:05,713
Look for it in the corner.

412
00:29:05,880 --> 00:29:08,480
That is why they still
keep an eye on his house.

413
00:29:09,453 --> 00:29:11,067
They track every
move his family makes.

414
00:29:14,033 --> 00:29:16,327
Was Pankaj... your friend?

415
00:29:17,693 --> 00:29:18,700
Iraboty?

416
00:29:20,720 --> 00:29:23,420
And you want justice for
him and his village.

417
00:29:27,207 --> 00:29:31,286
The evidence these MLA's
are looking for to destroy it.

418
00:29:31,833 --> 00:29:33,473
You are looking for
the same evidence...

419
00:29:34,373 --> 00:29:35,787
to show it to the world.

420
00:29:38,027 --> 00:29:41,427
But neither you nor they
have found that evidence.

421
00:29:44,373 --> 00:29:48,080
You will release those
video tapes through the media...

422
00:29:49,580 --> 00:29:52,307
so that, even if you
don't get justice

423
00:29:54,020 --> 00:29:55,620
at least their names
will be tarnished.

424
00:29:55,933 --> 00:29:57,253
I don't want their names tarnished
I want them punished.

425
00:29:59,527 --> 00:30:01,833
They will just claim
that this is not them.

426
00:30:02,340 --> 00:30:03,326
It's a doctored tape.

427
00:30:03,350 --> 00:30:06,095
The truth will be revealed
once an investigation starts.

428
00:30:06,120 --> 00:30:07,480
If there even is an investigation.

429
00:30:12,153 --> 00:30:15,860
When was the last time
you spoke to Pankaj?

430
00:30:19,287 --> 00:30:20,733
On the day of the protest.

431
00:30:22,113 --> 00:30:23,280
He was scared.

432
00:30:24,347 --> 00:30:26,907
He said he has proof
and his life is in danger.

433
00:30:28,340 --> 00:30:32,020
I said you should leave town for
a few days, I will help you.

434
00:30:33,213 --> 00:30:34,327
He agreed.

435
00:30:35,093 --> 00:30:36,840
He said I just need to
meet my mother once.

436
00:30:39,207 --> 00:30:40,300
And then...

437
00:30:47,180 --> 00:30:49,633
I... I hate tears Pushpa.

438
00:30:54,640 --> 00:30:56,473
Where are you going?
Do you have an idea?

439
00:30:57,160 --> 00:30:58,247
Yes...

440
00:30:59,307 --> 00:31:00,520
I have a mother.

441
00:31:05,713 --> 00:31:09,027
Hey soldier, it's just two people.
You want to try fighting them?

442
00:31:10,267 --> 00:31:11,886
Have you lost your mind?
Do you want to die?

443
00:31:11,987 --> 00:31:13,033
What happened?

444
00:31:13,920 --> 00:31:14,836
There are people there.

445
00:31:14,860 --> 00:31:16,340
We need to find
an alternative route.

446
00:31:16,687 --> 00:31:18,747
-It's right here. Let's go.
-Wait. Wait a minute.

447
00:31:20,067 --> 00:31:21,453
What?

448
00:31:23,433 --> 00:31:24,660
Did you call him?

449
00:31:27,113 --> 00:31:29,567
Great, so now we are
working with the blackmailer?

450
00:31:30,067 --> 00:31:31,220
And who is he?

451
00:31:31,480 --> 00:31:32,653
This is Bhombol.

452
00:31:33,507 --> 00:31:34,853
So you're here.

453
00:31:35,433 --> 00:31:36,560
Did you come alone?

454
00:31:36,613 --> 00:31:39,680
But sir you forgot to give me the order
of bringing the battalion with me.

455
00:31:41,213 --> 00:31:42,473
-I have this with me.
-Okay, okay.

456
00:31:42,580 --> 00:31:44,773
We cannot put Pankaj's family
in any more danger. Please leave.

457
00:31:44,827 --> 00:31:49,207
Helping Pankaj's family cross
the border is your responsibility.

458
00:31:49,327 --> 00:31:51,573
You have to give them a
home and a new identity.

459
00:31:52,780 --> 00:31:53,940
Deal?

460
00:31:54,780 --> 00:31:56,107
Come here.

461
00:31:57,653 --> 00:31:59,827
What is wrong with you?
Creating a new mess?

462
00:32:00,220 --> 00:32:02,607
Your job was to catch the blackmailer.
Which you did. That's finished--

463
00:32:02,632 --> 00:32:05,136
My job is not to
catch the blackmailer,

464
00:32:05,160 --> 00:32:07,333
my job is to catch the criminal. And those
three MLA's are the criminals. Not Iraboty.

465
00:32:07,460 --> 00:32:08,900
You can decide
whose side you are on.

466
00:32:09,353 --> 00:32:11,046
-You're making a mistake again--
-I am not making any mistake.

467
00:32:11,120 --> 00:32:12,159
I am going.

468
00:32:12,267 --> 00:32:13,627
And if anything happens to me...

469
00:32:14,087 --> 00:32:15,927
then you will have to inform mom.

470
00:32:28,127 --> 00:32:30,413
Aunty... Um... Mausi...

471
00:32:30,940 --> 00:32:31,940
Vasudha ji!

472
00:32:33,447 --> 00:32:37,533
Did Pankaj meet you
before he passed away?

473
00:32:39,427 --> 00:32:41,360
I mean... what did he say exactly?

474
00:32:43,167 --> 00:32:44,267
He said...

475
00:32:45,233 --> 00:32:50,133
"Ma, I will be leaving
for a few days.

476
00:32:51,040 --> 00:32:53,100
Make sure to have
your medicine on time.

477
00:32:53,987 --> 00:32:57,300
Help Trisha prepare
for her UPSC exam."

478
00:32:57,620 --> 00:32:59,440
His books are still here

479
00:32:59,553 --> 00:33:03,207
and he said, "Those would
help her in her studies."

480
00:33:03,550 --> 00:33:04,877
In her studies...

481
00:33:07,246 --> 00:33:08,499
My son...

482
00:33:23,440 --> 00:33:25,127
-Trisha? Trisha?
-Yes.

483
00:33:25,607 --> 00:33:28,007
Are these all the books?
They are not enough.

484
00:33:28,247 --> 00:33:29,467
Are there any more books?

485
00:33:30,207 --> 00:33:32,227
Yes, there are more books inside.

486
00:33:32,547 --> 00:33:34,473
Really? There are more?
Can I see them?

487
00:33:35,340 --> 00:33:37,007
Encyclopedia Britannica.

488
00:33:37,773 --> 00:33:39,360
It's very useful for UPSC.

489
00:33:40,020 --> 00:33:41,407
What subjects are you studying?

490
00:33:42,187 --> 00:33:44,647
Public administration and
Public affairs.

491
00:33:44,700 --> 00:33:46,633
Edition 15 and volume 17.

492
00:33:47,560 --> 00:33:48,727
Easy marks.

493
00:33:51,807 --> 00:33:53,420
Volume 17...

494
00:34:43,167 --> 00:34:44,913
Now we just need to get
them out of here safely.

495
00:34:45,527 --> 00:34:46,880
Something is missing, right?

496
00:34:47,173 --> 00:34:48,125
What?

497
00:34:48,150 --> 00:34:50,046
Lipstick, should I ask Ira?

498
00:34:50,467 --> 00:34:51,973
Do you think this is
'Jaane Bhi Do Yaaron's climax?

499
00:34:52,060 --> 00:34:55,620
'Jaane Bhi Do Yaaron'?
You are still young...

500
00:34:59,613 --> 00:35:00,860
Hey look at that!

501
00:35:02,660 --> 00:35:03,747
Stop them!

502
00:35:18,533 --> 00:35:19,693
Okay?

503
00:35:43,013 --> 00:35:44,108
Take a left from here.

504
00:35:44,133 --> 00:35:45,565
But this is a jungle
what are you saying?

505
00:35:45,589 --> 00:35:46,913
Shekhar take a left, listen to me.

506
00:35:47,080 --> 00:35:48,278
-Here!
-Don't touch the steering!

507
00:35:48,302 --> 00:35:49,500
What are you doing Iraboty?

508
00:35:55,033 --> 00:35:56,240
Shit!

509
00:35:56,653 --> 00:35:58,093
Stop here Shekhar!

510
00:35:58,167 --> 00:35:59,333
-Stop!
-No, we can't stop here.

511
00:35:59,358 --> 00:36:00,720
What are you doing Iraboty?

512
00:36:02,693 --> 00:36:03,747
Have you lost your mind?

513
00:36:03,827 --> 00:36:06,393
What are you doing?
This is sui... sui...

514
00:37:19,390 --> 00:37:20,624
For you.

515
00:37:28,280 --> 00:37:29,447
Thank you.

516
00:37:31,180 --> 00:37:32,460
Will we see each other soon?

517
00:37:33,790 --> 00:37:34,857
I doubt it.

518
00:37:37,487 --> 00:37:38,647
Are you sure?

519
00:37:57,350 --> 00:37:59,586
HEAVY ALLEGATIONS AGAINST STATE
GOVERNMENT MLAs, ARRESTED FOR MASSACRE

